# A top-level function whose result is a comparison's, used only as a
# number or a condition, returns Int (T10, X_eTaL-libraries' X17): the
# variable is settled when the definition is generalized. One that
# also appears in an argument stays open, a condition that is never a
# number (Truthy alone) stays one, so each use makes it a Bool or an
# Int, and inside a definition a comparison is still a Bool in a guard
# and an Int in arithmetic.
== SOURCE
u:a_nd := { a b -> 2 d_ecode (2 2 2 2 e_ncode a) & 2 2 2 2 e_ncode b }
u:p_os := { x -> x > 0 }
u:s_ame := { x -> x }
12 u:a_nd 10
u:p_os 3
(u:p_os 3) + 1
u:s_ign := { x -> u:p_os x ? "yes"; "no" }
u:s_ign 3
== TYPE
u:a_nd : Int -> Int -> Int
u:p_os : (Num a, Truthy b) => a -> b
u:s_ame : Any a => a -> a
Int
Bool
Int
u:s_ign : Num a => a -> Char
Char
== RESULT
8
1
2
yes
